WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Touch a Mimosa leaf, and its
leaflets fold up within seconds.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:10.600
In 1926, rice seedlings struck by a
fungus were found growing abnormally tall:

3
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.730
foolish seedling disease.

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.490
And every year, a plant
must time its biggest steps:

5
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.940
a seed waking, a flower
opening, a fruit ripening.

6
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.180
With no brain or nerves, how does
a plant know when to wake a seed,

7
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.780
open a flower or ripen its fruit?

8
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.190
In this mission, you'll take
key moments like these apart,

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.820
step by step.

10
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.900
Then you'll use the evidence to
work out what is really in control.

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.130
Your mission: find out how a
plant, with no brain or nerves,

12
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.960
times a seed, a flower and a fruit.
